  "question": {
    "text": "A line passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and is parallel to the vector <math><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>.</mo></math> If <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>P</mi></math> is a point on this line such that <math><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></math>, then the coordinates of point <math><mi>P</mi></math> can be&nbsp;"
